## Sibling file drift note (regression_bugs, pre-existing, NOT this diff)
Admin/app/CentralLogics/helpers.php::sendNotificationToHttp (already-fixed
prior ticket, untouched by NEARS-2428) logs the full raw $data array
(including message.token) on its 'config missing' / 'access token null'
paths, and $response->body() on its failure path - both violate the
logging-contract "never log request payload/token/response body" rule.
Also uses Log::info() for its own success line, so it is affected by the
same LOG_LEVEL=warning filtering documented above. Flagged separately as
regression_bugs - not introduced by, and not in scope of, this ticket's diff.
